# 162 - Talent Tree Analysis Script

## Status
- Created: 2026-04-05
- Phase: 2
- Priority: Medium

## Current Behavior
- No automated way to analyze talent point budgets per class
- Manual counting required to verify tier limits provide enough options
- Custom classes have no tooling to verify talent arrangement

## Intended Behavior
- CLI script that analyzes talent trees for any class
- Outputs 3 tables (one per talent tree)
- Shows total talent point options per tree and overall
- Supports both base WoW classes and custom classes
- Helps verify 60-point budget against ~80-120 available options

## Script Specification

### Usage
```bash
# Base class analysis
./scripts/analyze-talents.lua --class warrior
./scripts/analyze-talents.lua --class paladin --tiers 3

# Custom class analysis
./scripts/analyze-talents.lua --class knight --custom

# All classes summary
./scripts/analyze-talents.lua --all --tiers 3
```

### Command Line Flags
| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--class <name>` | Class to analyze (warrior, paladin, hunter, etc.) |
| `--custom` | Treat class as custom class (look in custom-classes.lua) |
| `--tiers <n>` | Limit analysis to first n tiers (default: 3) |
| `--all` | Analyze all classes and show summary |
| `--verbose` | Show individual talent descriptions |

