## Data Sources

### Base Classes
- Read from WoW DBC files or wowhead scraping
- Or hardcode tier 1-3 talents per class (simpler)
- Reference: https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/talent-calc

### Custom Classes
- Read from `src/lua/custom-classes.lua`
- Parse the talent definitions with tier/tree assignments
- Requires custom classes to define tree structure

## Implementation Steps

1. Create script skeleton with CLI argument parsing
2. Hardcode base class tier 1-3 talent data (manual from wowhead)
3. Add custom class parser for custom-classes.lua
4. Implement table formatting and summary calculation
5. Add --all flag for batch analysis
6. Test with Knight custom class

